9. WHAT I WOULD IMPROVE WITH MORE TIME
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  Priority 1: Larger, Higher-Quality Dataset (Impact: HIGH)
  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Target: 5,000-50,000 instruction-response pairs
  Sources:
  • AI4Bharat Samanantar: 47M Sanskrit-English sentence pairs
  • Sanskrit Wikipedia → explanation task generation
  • GRETIL digital library → verse + commentary pairs
  • Synthetic generation via GPT-4 for grammar tasks
  
  This is the single highest-leverage improvement available.

  Priority 2: Sanskrit-Specific Tokenizer (Impact: HIGH)
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Train a SentencePiece tokenizer on a large Sanskrit corpus:
  • Include Devanagari Unicode blocks
  • Cover common sandhi patterns
  • Add IAST diacritics
  
  Then: resize the model's embedding matrix and initialize new
  token embeddings via vocabulary transfer (average of similar
  Unicode character embeddings).
  
  Expected improvement: 2× token efficiency → more content in context

  Priority 3: Better Base Model (Impact: MEDIUM-HIGH)
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  • Sarvam-1B: Specifically trained for Indic languages including Sanskrit
  • ai4bharat/Airavata: Instruction-tuned for Indic languages
  • These would provide better Devanagari understanding out of the box

  Priority 4: RLHF / DPO Alignment (Impact: MEDIUM)
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  After supervised fine-tuning, use DPO (Direct Preference Optimization)
  with human preference data:
  • Ask Sanskrit scholars to rank model outputs
  • DPO training to prefer accurate translations over hallucinations
  
  This would significantly reduce hallucination rates.

  Priority 5: Structured Evaluation Benchmark (Impact: MEDIUM)
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Create a proper held-out test set:
  • 500 Sanskrit → English translations with multiple references
  • 100 grammar questions with expert-verified answers
  • 50 verse explanations graded by Sanskrit scholars
  
  Use chrF++ for script-aware evaluation + human evaluation.

  Priority 6: Retrieval Augmentation (Impact: MEDIUM)
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  For factual queries, augment generation with:
  • Vector database of Sanskrit texts + commentaries
  • Retrieve relevant verse/commentary before generating
  • This grounds responses in actual texts, reducing hallucination
  
  Would be especially valuable for verse identification tasks.

  Priority 7: Flash Attention + Longer Context (Impact: LOW-MEDIUM)
  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Flash Attention 2 would allow:
  • Longer max_seq_length (1024+) for multi-verse texts
  • Faster training on L4/A100
  • Better handling of long Sanskrit passages

