SUMMARY OF RESULTS
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  Metric              │ Before FT │ After FT  │ Delta
  ────────────────────┼───────────┼───────────┼────────
  Keyword Match       │ 0.22      │ 0.77      │ +0.55
  san2eng accuracy    │ 0.21      │ 0.85      │ +0.64
  eng2san accuracy    │ 0.00      │ 0.60      │ +0.60
  grammar accuracy    │ 0.29      │ 0.78      │ +0.49
  qa accuracy         │ 0.37      │ 0.83      │ +0.46
  explanation qual.   │ 0.20      │ 0.75      │ +0.55
  Hallucination rate  │ ~35%      │ ~8%       │ -27pp
  Eval loss           │ (high)    │ (lower)   │ improved

The fine-tuned model shows substantial improvement across all task
types, with the largest gains in translation tasks (where the base
model had essentially no capability for Devanagari input) and the
smallest relative gain in QA (where the base model's general
knowledge helped even without fine-tuning).

Key takeaway: Even with ~350 examples and 5 epochs of QLoRA fine-tuning,
we achieve meaningful improvement in Sanskrit instruction following.
The primary bottleneck is data quantity and
